      {
        "id": 134872,
        "name": "JimB",
        "username": "JimB",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jimb/{size}/2093_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-03-08T01:36:17.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"TheRadGasm\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/theradgasm/48/2271_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TheRadGasm:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Could we have done better?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Anything’s possible, but I have to say, the only Dark Watch power I like is Expatriette’s, and there is no environment I hate more than Rook City.  I find Dark Watch Setback crippled by a lack of a base power that can give him Unlucky Tokens, Dark Watch Nightmist severely hampered by losing a power that gets cards into her greedy little hands, and all teams hampered by Dark Watch Mister Fixer breaking their stuff (though to be fair, if you have to break anyone’s stuff, Setback is the most likely to profit from the deal; throw out a “High Risk Behavior” long enough to hit someone really hard, then have Dark Watch Mister Fixer break it before you can get bitten by it).</p>\n<p>I feel like the odds were against you.  Too much of your time was being spent in set-up, and you had too little damage going out.</p>",
        "post_number": 7,
        "post_type": 1,
